    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Test cleanup removes a hardcoded \"alias\" IDP instead of the IDPs the test created",
      "description": "The loop in `testCacheIDPForLogin` registers `getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(\"alias\")::remove);` on every iteration. The literal `\"alias\"` is not the alias of any IDP the test creates (`\"idp-alias-\" + i`), so the cleanup never removes the 20 IDPs. The same mistake appears for `idp-alias-20` a few lines later in the new test. The cleanup should target the created alias, for example `\"idp-alias-\" + i` and `\"idp-alias-\" + 20`. As written, the IDPs leak into other tests that share the realm.",
